<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cleartext is permitted app-wide, deliberately.

  The app's ONLY network activity is LAN sync with the desktop app over
  ws://<pc-ip>:9847 — there is no analytics, no remote API, no update check and
  no ad SDK (grep for OkHttp usage: SyncManager is the sole caller).

  A previous revision tried to narrow this to private ranges with
  <domain-config> entries like 10.0.0.0/8. That does NOT work: Android's
  network-security-config matches <domain> values as hostnames, not CIDR blocks,
  so the ranges never matched and every sync failed with
  "CLEARTEXT communication to 10.0.2.2 not permitted by network security policy".
  Android provides no way to scope cleartext to a subnet, so the choice is
  app-wide cleartext or no LAN sync at all.

  What protects the channel instead: the desktop refuses every read and write
  until the client presents the pairing code shown in its sidebar. That is access
  control, not confidentiality — see the security note in README.md.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
